---
layout: base.njk
title: "AEO Audit: ASW Hub vs. Unstructured Content"
description: "Live before/after citation rates for Airspace World 2026 content across ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews, Claude, Copilot, and Gemini. Updated monthly."
permalink: /aeo-audit-hub/
schemaFaq: true
---

<div class="audit-page">
  <div class="container">

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="audit-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">AEO Audit · Updated {{ audit.lastUpdated }}</p>
      <h1>How visible is ASW 2026 content<br>across every major AI engine?</h1>
      <p class="audit-lede">This page publishes the hub's own citation audit — before and after structured AEO content was applied. Five standard queries. Six engines. Real results, updated monthly. This is Maxifi's methodology working in public.</p>
      <div class="audit-meta-row">
        <span class="audit-chip">{{ audit.summary.queriesTested }} queries tested</span>
        <span class="audit-chip">{{ audit.summary.enginesTracked }} engines tracked</span>
        <span class="audit-chip audit-chip--highlight">Updated {{ audit.lastUpdated }}</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Methodology note -->
    <div class="audit-methodology">
      <p class="audit-methodology-label">Methodology</p>
      <p>{{ audit.methodology }}</p>
      <p class="audit-methodology-queries-label">Standard test queries:</p>
      <ol class="audit-queries-list">
        {% for q in audit.queries %}
          <li>{{ q }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <!-- Before / After explainer -->
    <div class="audit-explainer">
      <div class="audit-explainer-col audit-explainer-before">
        <p class="audit-explainer-label audit-explainer-label--before">Before</p>
        <p class="audit-explainer-site">CANSO / Official ASW site</p>
        <p>Unstructured content. No Schema.org markup. No FAQ schema. No entity-rich H2 structure. No llms.txt. AI engines could not reliably extract answers about sessions, speakers, or themes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="audit-explainer-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
      <div class="audit-explainer-col audit-explainer-after">
        <p class="audit-explainer-label audit-explainer-label--after">After</p>
        <p class="audit-explainer-site">ASW Hub (this site)</p>
        <p>Schema.org Event, Person, and Article markup on every page. FAQPage schema on theme pages. Entity-rich H2 headings. Structured speaker and session data. llms.txt for AI crawlers. Citation report updated monthly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Engine results grid -->
    <section class="audit-results">
      <h2>Citation rates by engine</h2>
      <p class="audit-results-note">Each score = percentage of the 5 standard queries where the hub was cited or its content quoted verbatim in the AI answer.</p>

      <div class="audit-engine-grid">
        {% for engine in audit.engines %}
        <div class="audit-engine-card {% if engine.status == 'pending' %}audit-engine-card--pending{% endif %}">
          <div class="audit-engine-header">
            <div>
              <p class="audit-engine-name">{{ engine.name }}</p>
              <p class="audit-engine-vendor">{{ engine.vendor }}</p>
            </div>
            {% if engine.status == 'pending' %}
              <span class="audit-status-badge audit-status-badge--pending">Pending</span>
            {% elif engine.status == 'citing' %}
              <span class="audit-status-badge audit-status-badge--citing">Citing</span>
            {% else %}
              <span class="audit-status-badge audit-status-badge--not-yet">Not yet</span>
            {% endif %}
          </div>

          <div class="audit-bar-block">
            <div class="audit-bar-row">
              <span class="audit-bar-label">Before</span>
              <div class="audit-bar-track">
                <div class="audit-bar-fill audit-bar-fill--before" style="width: {{ engine.before }}%"></div>
              </div>
              <span class="audit-bar-pct">{{ engine.before }}%</span>
            </div>
            <div class="audit-bar-row">
              <span class="audit-bar-label">After</span>
              <div class="audit-bar-track">
                <div class="audit-bar-fill audit-bar-fill--after" style="width: {{ engine.after }}%"></div>
              </div>
              <span class="audit-bar-pct">{{ engine.after }}%</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          {% if engine.notes %}
          <p class="audit-engine-notes">{{ engine.notes }}</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What the numbers mean -->
    <section class="audit-faq">
      <h2>What do these numbers mean?</h2>

      <div class="audit-faq-item">
        <h3>What counts as a citation?</h3>
        <p>A citation is recorded when an AI engine either (a) links directly to a page on this hub, or (b) quotes content from this hub verbatim in its answer — without necessarily attributing the source. Both are evidence that the engine indexed and trusted the content enough to use it.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="audit-faq-item">
        <h3>Why is the "before" score zero for most engines?</h3>
        <p>Before this hub launched, information about Airspace World 2026 sessions, speakers, and themes existed only on the official CANSO and ASW websites — presented as unstructured HTML with no Schema.org markup, no FAQ schema, and no entity-rich content architecture. AI engines could find the pages but could not reliably extract structured answers. The result: near-zero citation rates across all engines for the specific queries delegates and aviation professionals actually ask.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="audit-faq-item">
        <h3>How is the "after" score measured?</h3>
        <p>The five standard queries listed above are submitted manually to each engine on the first of every month. Results are recorded as cited (content from this hub appears in the answer) or not cited. The percentage shown is the share of queries where the hub was cited that month.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="audit-faq-item">
        <h3>Why do different engines show different scores?</h3>
        <p>Each AI engine has a different crawl schedule, indexing architecture, and citation preference. Perplexity indexes and cites new structured content fastest. Google AI Overviews is more conservative — it requires higher domain authority and Schema.org markup before surfacing a source. ChatGPT's browsing mode and Copilot depend on Bing's index. Claude prioritises structured, entity-rich content. Gemini draws from Google's index but applies additional quality filters.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="audit-faq-item">
        <h3>What is the methodology behind this hub?</h3>
        <p>Every page is built to Maxifi Digital's AEO (Answer Engine Optimisation) framework: Schema.org structured data on every page type (Event, Person, Article, FAQPage), entity-rich H2 headings that answer real queries, bidirectional cross-links between sessions and speakers, a dynamic sitemap, and an llms.txt file that guides AI crawlers. The full methodology is explained on the <a href="/how-it-works/">How It Works</a> page.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <div class="maxifi-cta">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Want this for your event or association?</p>
        <h2>Maxifi Digital builds content AI engines cite</h2>
        <p>This hub is a live demonstration of the AEO methodology. If you want your conference, association, or professional body to be the answer AI gives — not a competitor — book a 30-minute audit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="maxifi-cta-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://maxifidigital.com/services/aeo-audit/" rel="noopener">Book a free audit →</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/how-it-works/">See the methodology</a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
